# DIBAY Customer Communication HARD LOCK

Companion: `docs/customer-communication/dibay-customer-communication-ssot.md`  
Authority: `lib/admin/notification-campaigns/campaign-source-authority.ts`

## RULE 1
Official Notice must have `app_notices` original with `content_type=notice` (`app_notice_id` required).

## RULE 2
System Bulletin must have `app_notices` original with `content_type=system` (`app_notice_id` required).

## RULE 3
Marketing must have content bind **OR** approved internal landing (not bare `/notifications`).

## RULE 4
Campaign is **delivery authority**, not original content authority.

## RULE 5
New title/body-only official campaign (CASE C / Pure transport) is **FORBIDDEN**.

## RULE 6
Bell / Push / Full Inbox must resolve to the **same original** for bound campaigns.

## RULE 7
Notification Detail must not be the original for **new** official notice/system/marketing campaigns.

## RULE 8
Transactional system events may use `/notifications/{eventId}`.

## RULE 9
Inquiry and Direct Message never use Campaign as original.

## RULE 10
Inquiry → `/mypage/inquiries/{threadId}`. Message → `/mypage/inbox/{threadId}`.

## RULE 11
Old unbound rows may remain readable. **New unbound writes are forbidden** (create/send/test-send).

## RULE 12
No migration/schema change without evidence and explicit approval.

## RULE 13
Do not merge notice and system bulletin member domains.

## RULE 14
Do not classify inquiry/message as `campaignType: "system"` for convenience. Prefer event types + `supportKind`.

## Do not

- Reintroduce `[Pure transport] No linked post` as an official send path
- Weaken `validateOfficialCampaignSource` for “QA convenience”
- Add inquiry/message/cs as Notification Center filter tabs
- Treat `campaignType=system` alone as transactional
